  "description": "<p>When I run the ActiveFedora test suite I see this message dozens of times: </p>\n\n<p>```<br/>\nWARN 00:37:08.772 (DefaultMessageFactory) MessageFactory event UserData is empty!<br/>\n```</p>\n\n<p>What does it mean?  The warning doesn't tell me how to react, but it appears to be very important! <img class=\"emoticon\" src=\"/images/icons/emoticons/wink.png\" height=\"16\" width=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" border=\"0\"/></p>\n\n<p>See <a href=\"https://travis-ci.org/projecthydra/active_fedora/jobs/108171935#L282\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://travis-ci.org/projecthydra/active_fedora/jobs/108171935#L282</a></p>",
